  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Estimate the time it takes to send \\(60\\) blocks of data over a communications channel if each block consists of \\(512\\) “chunks” and the channel can transmit \\(120\\) chunks per second.",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.04\\) seconds",
    "B": "\\(0.4\\) seconds",
    "C": "\\(4\\) seconds",
    "D": "\\(4\\) minutes",
    "E": "\\(4\\) hours"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First count the chunks in all \\(60\\) blocks. Then divide by the number of chunks transmitted each second to find the time in seconds:\n\\[\n\\text{time}=\\frac{60\\cdot512}{120}=256\\text{ seconds}.\n\\]\nSince \\(1\\) minute is \\(60\\) seconds and\n\\[\n256=4\\cdot60+16,\n\\]\nthe exact time is \\(4\\) minutes \\(16\\) seconds. This is approximately \\(\\boxed{4\\text{ minutes}}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
